WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.134 --> 00:00:04.787
[MUSIC]

00:00:04.787 --> 00:00:07.929
To me, Black History Month is a time for
reflection and

00:00:07.929 --> 00:00:10.868
inspiration, reflecting
on the intellectual and

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:15.054
societal contributions that the black
community has made to the world.

00:00:15.054 --> 00:00:19.479
Reflecting on the visionaries who rallied
against seemingly insurmountable prejudice

00:00:19.479 --> 00:00:21.663
and violence to make those contributions.

00:00:21.663 --> 00:00:23.867
And reflecting on those
last along the way.

00:00:23.867 --> 00:00:26.971
This month reminds me that
the trials of our present will one

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:29.517
day become the reflections
of our tomorrow, and

00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:33.822
inspires me to seek to be counted among
those who have contributed to that future.

00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:37.768
[MUSIC]

00:00:37.768 --> 00:00:41.892
&gt;&gt; Black History Month is an occasion
to reflect on the struggle of the past

00:00:41.892 --> 00:00:46.361
generations for freedom, give thanks
to our ancestors for being brave, and

00:00:46.361 --> 00:00:51.059
appreciate the inspiring progress people
from the African diaspora have made.

00:00:51.059 --> 00:00:55.395
Without them, walls and
barriers would not have been broken down.

00:00:55.395 --> 00:01:00.670
Looking forward, we can learn from this as
we seek to make our future a better and

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:03.843
more inclusive one for
those who come after us.

00:01:03.843 --> 00:01:09.190
[MUSIC]

00:01:09.190 --> 00:01:12.676
&gt;&gt; Black History Month is a time for
me to reflect and celebrate.

00:01:12.676 --> 00:01:16.965
I reflect on the words 'in spite of'
when I think about Black History Month.

00:01:16.965 --> 00:01:21.466
I often think about the magnitude of what
Black people across generations have

00:01:21.466 --> 00:01:26.102
accomplished, almost always in spite of
something, whether it be adversity or

00:01:26.102 --> 00:01:27.895
a presumption of inequality.

00:01:27.895 --> 00:01:32.498
Black History Month is also a time when
I celebrate Black people's prevailing

00:01:32.498 --> 00:01:36.682
resilience and the vitality that
sustains our influential progress,

00:01:36.682 --> 00:01:38.017
creativity, and hope

00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:42.936
[MUSIC]

00:01:42.936 --> 00:01:47.853
&gt;&gt; Our world isn't perfect by any means,
but Black History Month provides

00:01:47.853 --> 00:01:51.890
a healthy blend of celebration and
reflective criticism.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:54.734
They may sound contradictory, but

00:01:54.734 --> 00:02:00.151
I found those two to be a necessary
pair for progress driven by hope.

00:02:00.151 --> 00:02:04.860
[MUSIC]

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:08.628
&gt;&gt; Black History Month is a time to
celebrate all the progress we've made,

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:12.396
while acknowledging the immense work
that still needs to be done to get to

00:02:12.396 --> 00:02:13.530
an equitable plane.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:17.159
It reminds us that progress is not linear,
but

00:02:17.159 --> 00:02:21.449
arcs towards justice with enough work and
sacrifice.

00:02:21.449 --> 00:02:25.438
It's a month of jubilation for
the progress we've made, sorrow for

00:02:25.438 --> 00:02:28.256
the leaders we've lost,
and hope that we can and

00:02:28.256 --> 00:02:31.787
will leave the world a better place for
future generations.

00:02:31.787 --> 00:02:36.715
[MUSIC]

00:02:36.715 --> 00:02:40.410
&gt;&gt; Black History Month has always
been a complex time for me.

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:44.813
A time for learning and celebration,
to build a deeper appreciation for

00:02:44.813 --> 00:02:48.869
the rich history and progress of
the African American community.

00:02:48.869 --> 00:02:52.689
A time for reflection,
to ask myself what more can I be doing for

00:02:52.689 --> 00:02:54.070
the Black community?

00:02:54.070 --> 00:02:58.556
And to also constructively challenge those
in positions of power around me to do more

00:02:58.556 --> 00:02:59.070
as well.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.829
And lastly, a time for
fellowship, to navigate

00:03:01.829 --> 00:03:06.541
all the complexities of the month with
a community that is incredibly supportive,

00:03:06.541 --> 00:03:09.452
and one that I could not be
more proud to be a part of.

00:03:09.452 --> 00:03:15.329
[MUSIC]

00:03:15.329 --> 00:03:20.122
&gt;&gt; Black History Month is a time to
remind myself of the sacrifices that were

00:03:20.122 --> 00:03:24.455
made by my ancestors, and
the many more that have come before me.

00:03:24.455 --> 00:03:29.401
It is a time to reflect on the reasons
why I have the privileges I do today, and

00:03:29.401 --> 00:03:32.666
the responsibilities that
are attached to them.

00:03:32.666 --> 00:03:36.870
It is a time to celebrate
the accomplishments of the American Negro

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:39.347
ethnicity in spite of the adversity and

00:03:39.347 --> 00:03:43.789
institutional challenges that have and
continue to work against it.

00:03:43.789 --> 00:03:49.724
[MUSIC]

00:03:49.724 --> 00:03:54.716
&gt;&gt; For me, Black History Month represents
a time of reflection about who

00:03:54.716 --> 00:03:57.263
I really am, and where I come from.

00:03:57.263 --> 00:04:02.908
As someone born in Africa, raised in
Canada, and now living in the US,

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:08.195
I have seen and experienced just
how varied Black identity can be.

00:04:08.195 --> 00:04:11.250
We are far from being a monolith.

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:17.155
And yet, we share a relentless spirit
that allows us to not just survive,

00:04:17.155 --> 00:04:21.740
no matter where we are, but
more importantly to thrive.

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:25.564
So, onwards and upwards we go.

00:04:25.564 --> 00:04:30.577
[MUSIC]

00:04:30.577 --> 00:04:35.456
&gt;&gt; To me, Black History Month is not only
a time to reflect on the sacrifices,

00:04:35.456 --> 00:04:39.574
resilience and accomplishments
of those that came before us.

00:04:39.574 --> 00:04:42.958
It's a time where I recognize and
celebrate the trials and

00:04:42.958 --> 00:04:46.353
progress we are making today for
our future generations.

00:04:46.353 --> 00:04:49.168
It's a reminder that we
should take time to reflect,

00:04:49.168 --> 00:04:51.933
celebrate ourselves and
not water ourselves down.

00:04:51.933 --> 00:04:56.520
[MUSIC]

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:01.465
&gt;&gt; Black History Month for me is
a celebration of Blackness, our successes,

00:05:01.465 --> 00:05:05.388
our wins, our progress,
our contributions to the world,

00:05:05.388 --> 00:05:08.859
our multifaceted and
diverse history and stories.

00:05:08.859 --> 00:05:11.917
It's also about reflecting on
our progress through adversity,

00:05:11.917 --> 00:05:14.873
while looking ahead to all the work
that still needs to be done.

00:05:14.873 --> 00:05:19.569
[MUSIC]

00:05:19.569 --> 00:05:24.028
&gt;&gt; Black History Month means
making space to pause,

00:05:24.028 --> 00:05:27.432
reflect, celebrate, and connect.

00:05:27.432 --> 00:05:33.595
It means acknowledging and celebrating
the resilience and beauty of Black people.

00:05:33.595 --> 00:05:36.336
It means reflecting on Black history, and

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:40.689
thinking about what I can do to
shaped Black futures for the better.

00:05:40.689 --> 00:05:49.139
[MUSIC]

